@packages/compiler import { SigilAgentAdapter, SigilAgentAdapterExecutionCoordinator, SigilAgentAdapterSubprocess, SigilAgentEvaluationRequest }

component SigilClaudeCompilerAdapter {
  goal {
    Execute provider-neutral compiler evaluation through the Claude Code CLI and
    return one validated result under an ephemeral, best-effort read-only
    inspection policy with model-mediated Bash risk.
  }

  interface {
    ClaudeAdapter {
      evaluate(SigilAgentEvaluationRequest) implements SigilAgentAdapter for provider
      claude with implementation identity builtin.claude-cli and the exact adapter
      package version

      provider-specific declarations match capabilities schemaVersion 1 with
      read-only workspace access, no agent-tool network, no approval escalation, and
      ephemeral state persistence.

      Observability declares no progress, partial usage, final cost, and
      post-settlement-only token and cost budget enforcement.
    }
  }
}

expand SigilClaudeCompilerAdapter {
  logic {
    ClaudeAdapter {
      Consume the provider-neutral request validation and capability-match result
      before invocation. Send one stream-json user message through claude print mode
      with the selected workspace, optional model, plan permissions, explicit
      read-only tools, safe startup, and disabled session persistence.

      The user message carries evaluationPrompt output unchanged. That provider-
      neutral envelope preserves stage, target identity, purpose, selected retrieval
      evidence, evaluator guidance, command policy, findings schema, and result
      instructions; capability, budget, and snapshot fields remain control metadata.

      Supply Claude execution and cleanup hooks to
      SigilAgentAdapterExecutionCoordinator and use SigilAgentAdapterSubprocess for
      the private process lifecycle. Parse the complete JSONL stream and require
      exactly one successful result event. Its result text must be one findings JSON
      object, optionally enclosed by one Markdown code fence; surrounding narration,
      multiple JSON values, malformed JSON, and trailing content are rejected as
      final-result-protocol.

      Aggregate numeric input_tokens, output_tokens, and cache_read_input_tokens from
      assistant message usage blocks. Missing or malformed usage fields remain
      unavailable; take total_cost_usd only from the successful result event, and
      leave cost unavailable when that field is absent or nonnumeric.
    }
  }

  constraints {
    ClaudeExecutionBoundary {
      Enable Read, Glob, Grep, and Bash for the compiler's best-effort read-only
      inspection policy. Deny Edit, Write, and NotebookEdit; use plan permission mode
      and safe startup so project instructions, plugins, hooks, and MCP configuration
      do not widen the evaluation boundary while provider authentication remains
      available.

      Use --no-session-persistence and never resume, continue, fork, or reuse a prior
      Claude session. Declare ephemeral state and keep provider tool network
      disabled.

      Accept only one result event with subtype success. An unsuccessful result is
      execution; zero or multiple result events, missing result text, malformed
      result text, or invalid findings content are final-result-protocol.

      Malformed JSONL, non-object frames, and malformed assistant tool-use frames are
      final-result-protocol. Valid unsupported event types are ignored, while valid
      assistant tool-use blocks become started command observations.
    }
  }

  decisions {
    EphemeralClaudeExecution {
      Decision: Use Claude Code's --no-session-persistence flag and declare ephemeral
      state for compiler evaluations.

      Scope: Governs Claude invocation and consumes provider-neutral capability
      matching; excludes provider authentication and unrelated interactive Claude
      sessions.

      Trade-offs: Callers cannot resume an evaluation through Claude session storage.

      Discarded alternatives: Persistent state like OpenCode was rejected because the
      Claude CLI exposes an explicit non-persistence mode.

      Consequences: Each evaluation starts a fresh provider session and leaves no
      provider session record for the compiler to resume.
    }

    ReadOnlyClaudeTools {
      Decision: Use plan mode with explicit Read, Glob, Grep, and Bash tools while
      denying mutation tools and relying on the evaluator prompt for shell command
      policy.

      Scope: Governs Claude Code permissions for compiler evaluations; excludes
      operating-system sandboxing, provider authentication, and the provider-neutral
      command-policy owner.

      Trade-offs: Bash remains a model-mediated boundary, so command-family
      compliance depends on the evaluator following the read-only policy.

      Discarded alternatives: Disabling Bash was rejected because compiler inspection
      guidance includes sigil, rg, sed, and git command families.
    }

    ClaudeResultEvent {
      Decision: Select the single successful result event as the terminal assistant
      output and retain assistant tool-use blocks as command observations.

      Scope: Governs Claude stream-json parsing; excludes request validation and
      subprocess cleanup.

      Consequences: Partial assistant narration cannot satisfy the final-result
      protocol, and execution error result subtypes remain failures.
    }
  }

  cases {
    ClaudeAdapter {
      An ephemeral request invokes claude once and accepts one successful result
      after process and output settlement.

      A persistent request mismatches before invocation.

      Read and inspection tools remain available while edit and write tools are
      denied.

      An unsuccessful result subtype is execution. Zero or multiple result events,
      missing result text, malformed or fenced-invalid result text, and invalid
      findings content are final-result-protocol.

      Timeout, cancellation, or process failure follows bounded subprocess cleanup.
    }
  }
}
